      "writtenOn": "2024-10-11T00:25:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I just noticed \"hal/mgmt.h\"\n\nwhere it says:\n\n```\n// This class provides an interface to interact with the kernel.\nclass Mgmt {\npublic:\n  uint16_t get_vs_opcode(uint16_t vendor_specification);\n};\n```\n\nThis is not the intended design of GD. Instead, OS-specific abstraction should stay in `packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/gd/os/` such as `packages/modules/Bluetooth/system/gd/os/rand.h` and each operating system\u0027s abstraction should be implemented in sub-directories like `linux_generic`\n\nand methods should be defined there. In this case, Mgmt() should be spelled out fully as something like `Management()` or more specific with singleton pattern like `Management::getInstance().getVendorSpecificCode(int)` instead of creating a new instance each time. \n\nCould we move `gd/hal/mgmt.h` to `gd/os` first before start using them in critical files like `hci_hal_android.cc`?\n\nThanks",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 161,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 161,
        "endChar": 89
      },
      "revId": "29af1076a9281a0850c5e9be23db98ce5197263e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
